M('i','k',"What happens if you try to create an object of an abstract class with new?","It does not compile","It compiles but fails at run time","It creates an empty object","It calls the first subclass","An abstract class is incomplete, so it can only be instantiated through a concrete subclass.")
M('i','k',"What does the final keyword do on a method?","The method cannot be overridden","The method cannot be called twice","The method must be static","The method is run last","final on a class prevents inheritance, on a variable prevents reassignment, and on a method prevents overriding.")
