JV('a','o',"What does this program print?",P('        System.out.println(1 + 2 + "" + 1 + 2);'),"312","1212","33","3 12","1 + 2 is evaluated first as numbers (3). Once a String is involved the remaining operands are appended.")
JV('a','o',"What does this program print?",P('        System.out.println(Math.round(-2.5) + " " + Math.round(2.5));'),"-2 3","-3 3","-2 2","-3 2","Math.round rounds halves towards positive infinity, so -2.5 becomes -2 and 2.5 becomes 3.")
topic('OOP')
JV('a','o',"What does this program print?",P('        new X();','','class X {\n    static { System.out.print("S"); }\n    { System.out.print("I"); }\n    X() { System.out.print("C"); }\n}'),"SIC","CIS","ISC","SCI","The static initialiser runs once when the class loads, then the instance initialiser, then the constructor body.")
JV('a','o',"What does this program print?",P('        f(null);','    static void f(Object o) { System.out.println("Object"); }\n    static void f(String s) { System.out.println("String"); }'),"String","Object","Compile error","NullPointerException","The compiler picks the most specific applicable overload, and String is more specific than Object.")
topic('Exceptions')
JV('a','o',"What does this program print?",P('        System.out.println(f());','    @SuppressWarnings("finally")\n    static int f() {\n        try { return 1; }\n        finally { return 2; }\n    }'),"2","1","3","Compile error","A return in finally overrides the value returned from try. It is considered bad practice.")
JV('a','o',"What does this program print?",P('        List<Integer> l = new ArrayList<>(List.of(1, 2, 3));\n        try {\n            for (Integer i : l) l.remove(i);\n        } catch (Exception e) {\n            System.out.println(e.getClass().getSimpleName());\n        }'),"ConcurrentModificationException","IndexOutOfBoundsException","NullPointerException","No output","Removing from a list while iterating it with a for-each loop makes the iterator detect the change and fail fast.")
JV('a','o',"What does this program print?",P('        try (R a = new R("A"); R b = new R("B")) {\n            System.out.print("body ");\n        }','','class R implements AutoCloseable {\n    String n;\n    R(String n) { this.n = n; }\n    public void close() { System.out.print("close" + n + " "); }\n}'),"body closeB closeA","body closeA closeB","closeA closeB body","body","Resources are closed in the reverse order of their creation, after the body has run.")
